WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.780
<v Narrator>Every call to a main line starts with a reason.

2
00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:11.820
<v Narrator>A phone menu makes the caller translate that reason into a number.

3
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.730
<v Narrator>This agent just asks.

4
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.440
<v Narrator>Calls arrive on a Teams phone number, through Teams Phone extensibility.

5
00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:29.677
<v Narrator>Azure Communication Services Call Automation bridges the audio to Voice Live,

6
00:00:29.757 --> 00:00:32.620
<v Narrator>where GPT Realtime holds the conversation.

7
00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.330
<v Narrator>Your server decides where the call goes, and Teams receives it with context.

8
00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:42.406
<v Narrator>Dana calls Contoso's main line. There's no menu.

9
00:00:42.486 --> 00:00:44.304
<v Narrator>She just says what she needs.

10
00:00:45.189 --> 00:00:48.660
<v Agent>Hi Dana, you've reached Contoso — I'm the automated assistant.

11
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.719
<v Agent>What can I help you with today?

12
00:00:52.053 --> 00:00:54.633
<v Dana>I was charged twice on my invoice

13
00:00:54.937 --> 00:00:58.277
<v Agent>It sounds like Billing is the right team for that — shall I put you through?

14
00:00:59.621 --> 00:01:03.082
<v Narrator>The model proposes Billing, with a confidence score.

15
00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:06.821
<v Narrator>The server, not the model, checks it against the gate.

16
00:01:07.573 --> 00:01:12.373
<v Narrator>Even above the gate, the agent confirms before it transfers. Watch the Teams panel.

17
00:01:13.215 --> 00:01:14.645
<v Dana>yes please

18
00:01:14.942 --> 00:01:16.892
<v Agent>Connecting you now to Billing.

19
00:01:18.252 --> 00:01:21.395
<v Narrator>Billing's Teams client rings with the reason for the call

20
00:01:21.475 --> 00:01:23.825
<v Narrator>and who's calling, flagged as unverified.

21
00:01:23.905 --> 00:01:26.682
<v Narrator>That context travels in the call's VoIP headers.

22
00:01:28.738 --> 00:01:31.074
<v Narrator>Some requests really are ambiguous.

23
00:01:31.154 --> 00:01:34.277
<v Narrator>Priya was charged for a renewal she didn't order.

24
00:01:34.357 --> 00:01:36.268
<v Narrator>Is that Sales, or Billing?

25
00:01:37.131 --> 00:01:40.569
<v Agent>Hi Priya, you've reached Contoso — I'm the automated assistant.

26
00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:42.581
<v Agent>What can I help you with today?

27
00:01:43.913 --> 00:01:47.043
<v Priya>I was charged for a renewal I did not order

28
00:01:47.335 --> 00:01:49.990
<v Agent>Sorry, I want to make sure I get you to the right place.

29
00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.505
<v Agent>Could you tell me a bit more about what you need?

30
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.195
<v Narrator>Sales scored 0.6, under the 0.75 gate.

31
00:01:57.275 --> 00:02:01.730
<v Narrator>So instead of guessing, the agent asks one question.

32
00:02:02.535 --> 00:02:04.855
<v Priya>the charge on my card is wrong

33
00:02:05.142 --> 00:02:08.482
<v Agent>It sounds like Billing is the right team for that — shall I put you through?

34
00:02:09.808 --> 00:02:11.318
<v Priya>yes

35
00:02:11.619 --> 00:02:13.569
<v Agent>Connecting you now to Billing.

36
00:02:14.921 --> 00:02:18.585
<v Narrator>A wrong transfer costs far more than one clarifying question.

37
00:02:18.665 --> 00:02:22.301
<v Narrator>And the gate is a number in config, not a line in a prompt.

38
00:02:24.368 --> 00:02:28.128
<v Narrator>The quickest way to lose a caller is to make them argue with a bot.

39
00:02:28.978 --> 00:02:31.886
<v Agent>Thanks for calling Contoso — I'm the automated assistant.

40
00:02:31.966 --> 00:02:33.758
<v Agent>What can I help you with today?

41
00:02:35.097 --> 00:02:37.227
<v Caller>can I just talk to a person

42
00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.430
<v Agent>Connecting you now to Reception.

43
00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:43.662
<v Narrator>Asking for a person goes straight to Reception.

44
00:02:43.742 --> 00:02:45.854
<v Narrator>No gate, and no “are you sure?”

45
00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:50.328
<v Narrator>Callers change their minds.

46
00:02:50.408 --> 00:02:53.820
<v Narrator>Marcus has a question about his invoice.

47
00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:58.072
<v Agent>Hi Marcus, you've reached Contoso — I'm the automated assistant.

48
00:02:58.152 --> 00:03:00.004
<v Agent>What can I help you with today?

49
00:03:01.313 --> 00:03:03.903
<v Marcus>I have a question about my invoice

50
00:03:04.195 --> 00:03:07.535
<v Agent>It sounds like Billing is the right team for that — shall I put you through?

51
00:03:08.892 --> 00:03:10.550
<v Narrator>Watch the bar under the gauge.

52
00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:13.432
<v Narrator>The transfer waits about a second before it dispatches,

53
00:03:13.512 --> 00:03:15.662
<v Narrator>and Marcus is about to change his mind.

54
00:03:16.477 --> 00:03:18.417
<v Marcus>yes please

55
00:03:18.726 --> 00:03:20.676
<v Agent>Connecting you now to Billing.

56
00:03:21.018 --> 00:03:23.248
<v Marcus>no wait, the portal is down

57
00:03:23.512 --> 00:03:26.942
<v Agent>It sounds like Support is the right team for that — shall I put you through?

58
00:03:28.286 --> 00:03:30.951
<v Narrator>The transfer to Billing was cancelled before it left,

59
00:03:31.031 --> 00:03:32.786
<v Narrator>and Support is offered instead.

60
00:03:33.621 --> 00:03:34.464
<v Marcus>yes

61
00:03:34.544 --> 00:03:36.224
<v Agent>Connecting you now to Support.

62
00:03:37.578 --> 00:03:41.364
<v Narrator>Cancelled inside the window, re-proposed, and re-confirmed.

63
00:03:41.444 --> 00:03:44.098
<v Narrator>The trail shows billing, then support.

64
00:03:46.141 --> 00:03:48.354
<v Narrator>Same server, 7:30 in the evening.

65
00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:50.391
<v Narrator>Billing keeps office hours.

66
00:03:51.268 --> 00:03:54.739
<v Agent>Hi Dana, you've reached Contoso — I'm the automated assistant.

67
00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:56.798
<v Agent>What can I help you with today?

68
00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:00.390
<v Dana>I have a question about my invoice

69
00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.010
<v Agent>It sounds like Billing is the right team for that — shall I put you through?

70
00:04:05.351 --> 00:04:08.183
<v Narrator>Billing is still the right team, but it's closed.

71
00:04:08.263 --> 00:04:12.811
<v Narrator>The server checks the hours, and Billing's after-hours rule is to take a message.

72
00:04:13.645 --> 00:04:14.406
<v Dana>yes

73
00:04:14.486 --> 00:04:16.041
<v Agent>Billing is closed at the moment.

74
00:04:16.121 --> 00:04:18.657
<v Agent>I can take a short message and make sure it reaches them

75
00:04:18.737 --> 00:04:20.536
<v Agent>— what would you like me to pass on?

76
00:04:21.832 --> 00:04:24.302
<v Dana>please call me back about the duplicate charge

77
00:04:24.585 --> 00:04:27.961
<v Agent>Thanks — I've passed that on to Billing, and they'll see it when they're back.

78
00:04:28.041 --> 00:04:29.005
<v Agent>Goodbye for now.

79
00:04:30.362 --> 00:04:32.228
<v Narrator>No transfer into an empty queue.

80
00:04:32.308 --> 00:04:36.542
<v Narrator>The message waits in the audit log, with its topic, for Billing in the morning.

81
00:04:38.588 --> 00:04:41.831
<v Narrator>And when speech doesn't work at all, a bad line,

82
00:04:41.911 --> 00:04:44.818
<v Narrator>a noisy room, the keypad is always there.

83
00:04:45.705 --> 00:04:48.613
<v Agent>Thanks for calling Contoso — I'm the automated assistant.

84
00:04:48.693 --> 00:04:50.485
<v Agent>What can I help you with today?

85
00:04:51.854 --> 00:04:54.509
<v Agent>Sorry, I want to make sure I get you to the right place.

86
00:04:54.589 --> 00:04:57.024
<v Agent>Could you tell me a bit more about what you need?

87
00:04:58.363 --> 00:05:00.986
<v Agent>Sorry — I want to get this right.

88
00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:03.424
<v Agent>Could you tell me a bit more?

89
00:05:03.504 --> 00:05:09.173
<v Agent>Or use the keypad: 1 for Sales, 2 for Support, 3 for Billing, 4 for Reception.

90
00:05:10.504 --> 00:05:14.364
<v Narrator>A keypress is unambiguous, so it routes without asking again.

91
00:05:15.242 --> 00:05:16.922
<v Agent>Connecting you now to Support.

92
00:05:18.271 --> 00:05:22.015
<v Narrator>And every call is audited: transfers, clarifying questions,

93
00:05:22.095 --> 00:05:25.291
<v Narrator>people requested, and how long it took to route.

94
00:05:27.963 --> 00:05:32.773
<v Narrator>Under the hood, the model's only power is to propose a route from a fixed list.

95
00:05:33.223 --> 00:05:37.665
<v Narrator>The server applies the confidence gate, the office hours, and the confirmation.

96
00:05:37.745 --> 00:05:42.163
<v Narrator>Then Call Automation transfers the call to the Teams queue, with its context.

97
00:05:42.613 --> 00:05:46.333
<v Narrator>Every failure path ends with a person, never a loop.

98
00:05:48.533 --> 00:05:51.061
<v Narrator>Making it yours is mostly configuration.

99
00:05:51.141 --> 00:05:53.996
<v Narrator>Your teams, how they're described, their hours

100
00:05:54.076 --> 00:05:56.930
<v Narrator>and after-hours rules all live in routes.json,

101
00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:59.673
<v Narrator>and the gate is one environment variable.

102
00:06:00.123 --> 00:06:01.388
<v Narrator>The spec, the tests

103
00:06:01.468 --> 00:06:05.603
<v Narrator>and this demo script give your coding agent the context to change the rest.

104
00:06:08.203 --> 00:06:09.815
<v Narrator>Intent-based call routing.

105
00:06:09.895 --> 00:06:14.173
<v Narrator>Run it in simulation in two minutes, then connect it to your own Teams number.
